                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/260: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-09T15:00:00-00:44">April 9, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:51 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. My 45, April 7, 7 p.m. Under Christy’s chairmanship, the Commission has
                    virtually completed its organization; and the plan of procedure it is adopting
                    gives it the broadest scope possible, which is very satisfactory. The Commission
                    is expecting to hold a preliminary hearing for about 2 weeks in Monrovia and
                    will then proceed to work in the field.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
